Dear Mike,

I tried to work around this with a help from colleague who understands data types better than me.
So, the script would now go like this:

Lisso.means <- lapply(coords.subset(ScapA, classifier$Species), FUN = mshape)
Lisso.means.array <- array (unlist( Lisso.means ), dim = c( 13, 3 , length (Lisso.means)))
dimnames(Lisso.means.array)[[3]] <-  unique (gsub (pattern = '[0-9]+', replacement = "", names (unlist( Lisso.means ))))
identical (dimnames (Lisso.means.array)[[3]], LissoPhy$tip.label)

dimnames(Lisso.means.array)
newOrder <- match (LissoPhy$tip.label, dimnames (Lisso.means.array)[[3]])
Lisso.means.array.ordered <-Lisso.means.array[,,newOrder]

And when I test the data after, I get positive results:

> identical (dimnames (Lisso.means.array.ordered)[[3]], LissoPhy$tip.label)

[1] TRUE

> class(Lisso.means.array.ordered)

[1] "array"

> is.numeric(Lisso.means.array.ordered)

[1] TRUE

However, when I try the physignal function

Lissosignal<-physignal(Lisso.means.array.ordered, LissoPhy, iter = 999, seed = NULL, print.progress = FALSE)

I get the error message again:

Error in h(simpleError(msg, call)) :

  error in evaluating the argument 'x' in selecting a method for function 'tcrossprod': non-numeric argument to mathematical function

Is there probably something else that causes the error? My tree is

> class (LissoPhy)

[1] "phylo"

But it is imported from a .nex file.

All the best,

Aleksandar

